
		WORD PERFECT KEYBOARD LAYOUT FOR VEDIT
		--------------------------------------

The Word Perfect layout comes close for the common cursor movement and editing
functions.

Major Differences:

1.  <ESC> pops up the menu system.

2.  <F1> performs only [CANCEL], <Ctrl-U> performs {EDIT, Undo, Line}.

3.  The block functions work differently. [BLOCK COPY] is assigned to both 
    <F9> and <Ctrl-F4>. [BLOCK MOVE] is assigned to <Alt-F9>. {BLOCK, Set 
    marker} is assigned to <Alt-F4>.

4.  <F7> brings up the {FILE} menu from which you can select "Exit" to save
    your file and exit back to DOS.

    Note:  [HELP] will first display the keyboard layout listed on the next 
	   page. However, the screen for "Built-in Keystroke Macros" will not 
	   be entirely correct. This can be corrected by editing the 
	   beginning of VHELP.HLP (VEDIT PLUS: VVHELP.HLP) which is an
	   explanation of the built-in keystroke macros.


		  KEYBOARD LAYOUT

"+" indicates functions not available on Word Perfect
"!" indicates functions which operate differently from Word Perfect


[BACKSPACE]		<Backspace>
[BLOCK COPY]	   !	<F9>			<Ctrl-F4>
[BLOCK MOVE]	   !	<Alt-F9>
[CANCEL]		<F1>
[CURSOR UP]		<Cursor Up>
[CURSOR DOWN]		<Cursor Down>
[CURSOR RIGHT]		<Cursor Right>
[CURSOR LEFT]		<Cursor Left>
[DELETE]		<Del>
[DEL PREV WORD]	   !	<Home> <Del>
[DEL NEXT WORD]    !	<Home> <Backspace>	<Ctrl-Bksp>
[ENTER CTRL]	   !	<Ctrl-Q>
[ERASE EOL]	    	<Ctrl-End>
[ERASE LINE]	   +	<Ctrl-Y>
[ESCAPE]	   +	Grey*
[HELP]			<F3>
[INDENT]	   	<F4>
[INSERT TOGGLE]	   	<Ins>
[LINE BEGIN]		<Home> <Cursor Left>
[LINE END]		<Home> <Cursor Right>
[MENU]		   +	<ESC>
[NEXT LINE]	   +	<Ctrl-J>		<Ctrl-Enter>
[NEXT PARA]	   +	<Ctrl-PgDn>
[NEXT TAB STOP]	   +	<Ctrl-T>
[NEXT WORD]		<Ctrl-Cursor Right>
[PAGE UP]		<PgUp>			Grey-
[PAGE DOWN]		<PgDn>			Grey+
[PREVIOUS PARA]	   +	<Ctrl-PgUp>
[PREVIOUS WORD]		<Ctrl-Cursor Left>
[REPEAT]	   !	<Ctrl-R>
[REPLACE]		<Alt-F2>
[SCREEN BEGIN]		<Home> <Cursor Up>
[SCREEN END]		<Home> <Cursor Down>
[SCROLL UP]	   +	<Ctrl-A>
[SCROLL DOWN]	   +	<Ctrl-F>
[SCROLL RIGHT]	   +	<Ctrl-D>
[SCROLL LEFT]	   +	<Ctrl-S>
[SEARCH]		<F2>
[SEARCH AGAIN]	   +	<Ctrl-F2>
[TAB CHARACTER]		--->|
[T-REG COPY]	   +	Available in BLOCK menu
[T-REG MOVE]	   +	Available in BLOCK menu
[T-REG INSERT]	   +	Available in BLOCK menu
[UNDENT]	   +	|<---	
[VISUAL ESCAPE]	   +	Available in ESCAPE menu
[VISUAL EXIT]	   +	<Ctrl-E>


Begin of file		<Home> <Home> <Cursor Up>
End of file		<Home> <Home> <Cursor Down>
{GOTO} menu		<Ctrl-Home>
{FILE} menu		<F5> or <F7>
{PRINT} menu		<Shft-F7>

Block On	     !	<Alt-F4>
Center line		<Shft-F6>
Enter date		<Shft-F5>
Execute Macro	     !  <Alt-F10>
Format paragraph	<Alt-F3>
Justification		<Ctrl-F8>
Print configuration	<Alt-F8>
Reverse search		<Shft-F2>
Undo line	     +  <Ctrl-U>

Save file and resume editing	<F10>

Switch/create edit buffer	<Shft-F3>	(Simultaneously edit files)
Open (edit) new file		<Shft-F10>	(Same buffer)
Open (edit) new file		<Alt-N>		(Same buffer)
Open (edit) new file	   +	<Alt-O>		(New buffer, same window)
Open (edit) new file	   +	<Alt-Y>		(New buffer, new window)

Toggle between files	   +	<Alt-T>
Toggle VGA/EGA line mode   +	<Alt-L>
Toggle text colors	   +	<Alt-J>
Start up Compiler Support  +	<Alt-I>

{Block}  Sub-menu	<Alt-B>		{Config} Sub-menu	<Alt-C>
{Edit}   Sub-menu	<Alt-E>		{File}   Sub-menu	<Alt-F>
{Goto}   Sub-menu	<Alt-G>		{Help}   Sub-menu	<Alt-H>
{Misc}   Sub-menu	<Alt-M>		{Print}  Sub-menu	<Alt-P>
{Search} Sub-menu	<Alt-S>		{Window} Sub-menu	<Alt-W>
